  = must: preserve this decision as a deferral, not a rejection of future operations adapters, telemetry, schedulers, process/GPU/model/job integrations, or machine-management capabilities
  = must: require a later explicit activation slice before adding package dependencies, lockfiles, imports from external machine-management packages, adapters, transports, UI surfaces, socket listeners, telemetry collectors, process controllers, GPU controllers, model runtime clients, job queue clients, credential readers, network mutators, or persistent operations automation
  = must: require a separate future source-preserved and SJS-processed live-control authority path before any live machine control can be reconsidered
  = must: keep SOP, SJS, completion reviews, accepted decision documents, tracked fixture sources, expected ledgers, and canonical specifications as source authority
  = must: treat operation requests, dry-run results, resource estimates, generated reports, adapter state, telemetry, human approvals, carrier messages, terminal output, and chat events as projections or evidence until rewritten into accepted SOP authority by a later reviewed process

