  = must: require adapter tests to prove user or agent interactions route back to operation request records, SOP-first interrupts, human approval reviews, resource safety reviews, dependency decisions, or completion reviews rather than direct mutation

& [FutureLiveControlAuthorityPath] is the only path by which live machine control may be reconsidered later
  + [required_future_step] is preserve new live-control source document
  + [required_future_step] is SJS-process new source into signed canonical safety authority
  + [required_future_step] is define target host inventory and resource API boundaries
  + [required_future_step] is define least-privilege credential and secret boundary
  + [required_future_step] is define network exposure boundary
  + [required_future_step] is define dry-run, rollback, abort, and monitoring proof
  + [required_future_step] is define explicit fresh scoped human approval and expiration rule
  + [required_future_step] is define emergency stop and revocation path
  + [required_future_step] is run completion review that explicitly accepts live-control scope
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on IR7 dry-run success
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on broad human approval
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on generated fixture success
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on terminal, chat, mailbox, IRC, Matrix, web, or Codex carrier state
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on this deferral decision as permission

  = must: require a future, separate authority path for any live-control capability
  = must: keep current IR7 work non-live even after IR7 implementation completion

& [AuthorityBoundaryAssessment: IR7OperationsAdapters] is the authority fit assessment for future operations surfaces
  + [fit_status] is future_adapter_candidates_preserved
  + [fit_reason] is process, GPU, model-runtime, job-queue, telemetry, scheduler, and machine-management integrations may become useful projections or controlled execution surfaces after authority-preserving boundaries exist
  + [mismatch_status] is authority_boundary_mismatch_if_used_directly_as_truth
  + [mismatch_reason] is resource telemetry, process state, GPU state, model runtime state, job queues, terminal output, chat commands, adapter callbacks, UI events, and generated dry-run results are projections or execution state rather than accepted SOP authority
  + [adapter_need] is map accepted LangSOP authority records into adapter inputs and map adapter outputs back into non-authoritative operation requests, resource safety reviews, refusal records, SOP-first interrupts, or completion reviews until accepted by SOP review

  = must: prevent telemetry availability, dry-run success, generated report success, approval display state, adapter callback success, UI click, chat command, or terminal output from satisfying readiness, completion review, source specification processing, dispatch authority, operations authority, or live-control gates by itself
  = must: preserve human approval and resource safety as reviewed SOP records rather than direct UI, transport, terminal, adapter, or dispatch effects

